From: Silvia <2824799@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 18:23:29 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: mediatek: xaga: add the MT6895 VCP multimedia platform

Add the MT6895 VCP (video co-processor) multimedia stack for the Xiaomi
Redmi Note 11T Pro / 11T Pro+ / POCO X4 GT (xaga):

  - remoteproc/mediatek: the MT6895 VCP transport and resource routing
  - soc/mediatek: the DVFSRC multimedia handover and the MT6895 DVFSRC
    regulator topology
  - media/mediatek/vcodec: VCP-backed H.264 encoder and decoder frontends,
    the shared DMA-BUF/layout ABI, diagnostics and host selftests
  - arm64: dts: describe the VCP multimedia platform, the codec OPPs and
    the clock/power domains
  - arm64: configs: xaga: build the VCP codec stack in

The codec, remoteproc and DVFS work is the MT6895 VCP contribution series;
it is integrated here together with the board fixups found during
bring-up:

  - restore the ten bootloader-owned reserved-memory regions and their
    node numbering and drop the stray debug_met_res-ram carveout.  The
    rewritten addresses left live ATF/TEE/SCP/SSPM regions unreserved, so
    the kernel allocated from them and a DMA engine later corrupted the
    live page tables.
  - restore the archived LK framebuffer tag (fps 6060 and its tail
    padding) and drop the board-wide 725 mV dvfsrc_vcore constraint;
    neither belongs to the VCP platform description.
  - trim the xaga.config handset block down to the VCP codec bits
    (media/V4L2, VIDEO_MEDIATEK_*, MTK_VCP_RPROC and MTK_SCP/RPMSG) and
    drop CONFIG_INITRAMFS_FORCE, keeping the embedded-initramfs and
    no-/lib/modules contract.
  - fix the SCP integration build failures introduced by the merge.

Co-authorized-by: Hecheng Yu <kde-yyds@qq.com>

Local selection: retain only the stateful VCP decoder frontend/backend,
bitstream helpers and transport API declarations. Import the decoder fixes
through the pinned reference below. No xaga board, encoder, regulator,
remoteproc implementation or DVFS policy is imported. SoC adaptation and
build integration follow separately.

